The temperature limit now depends on the provider. Five providers whose own API docs say 0–2 now accept up to 2.0; every other provider stays at 1.0 as before. It's committed as 58717a77 ("Fixes #1207") but not pushed yet. Build, the full test suite, clippy and fmt all pass.

What changed
• One function, temperature_max_for_provider in src/temperature_support.rs, sets the limit. Everything else reads it:
  • the startup clamp, whose warning now names the range, e.g. Temperature 1.5 is outside 0.0–1.0 for anthropic, clamping to 1.0
  • /config set temperature, which checks against the session's provider
  • config get / config show, which use the provider named in the config file (anthropic if none)
  • --help, the settable-keys text, and three docs pages
• Every agent build clamps again to its own provider's limit. I added this beyond the plan: without it, a session started on openai at 1.5 that falls back (or /provider-switches) to anthropic would send 1.5 to a provider that only accepts up to 1.0. Now it sends 1.0.

The table (each 2.0 row's source URL is in a code comment and in the commit body):
• 2.0: openai (OpenAI's published OpenAPI spec, since platform.openai.com returned 403), google, deepseek, groq, cerebras.
• 1.0, sourced: xai (its API accepts up to 2 but documents that it samples at most 1) and zai (documents 0–1).
• 1.0, not sourced: openrouter (the gateway takes 0–2, but the routed vendor's range varies), mistral (its docs give a recommendation, not a range), anthropic, bedrock, minimax, ollama, custom and unknown names.
• Does yoagent clamp? No. It sends the value as given (openai_compat.rs:529, google.rs:787), and the existing accepts_sampling_params drop is untouched.

How I checked it
• Tests: one row per provider plus edge cases (1.5 on openai stays 1.5, 2.5 becomes 2.0, 1.5 on anthropic becomes 1.0). Each of the three readers and the agent builders has its own tests too.
• Sabotage check: setting one 2.0 row back to 1.0 made 5 tests fail, and the file is restored.
• Real-binary probe (run right after cargo build, against a dead local URL):
  • openai at 1.5: no warning
  • anthropic at 1.5: clamp warning
  • openai at 2.5: clamps to 2.0

Still open, filed as #1208
• The limit follows the provider name, so provider = "openai" with a base_url pointing at some other server still gets 2.0.
• OpenRouter stays capped at 1.0 even for GPT or DeepSeek models routed through it.
• Google's docs say Gemini 3.6 Flash and newer silently ignore temperature. From yoagent's source, nothing drops it for those models, so users get no note. That's probably a fix for yoagent rather than yoyo.

The sourced table and the trace are also posted on #1207.

cli.rs, config.rs and agent_builder.rs grew 6, 33 and 13 lines. All three stay inside the size check's grace band, so I didn't change the recorded sizes in tests/module_size.rs.

